### Try the API from VS / VS Code / Rider (REST Client). Start the API first: dotnet run
@api = http://localhost:5080

### Health
GET {{api}}/api/health

### List employees (search + filter + sort + paging)
GET {{api}}/api/employees?search=a&sortBy=salary&sortDir=desc&page=1&pageSize=5

### One employee
GET {{api}}/api/employees/1

### Departments
GET {{api}}/api/departments

### Login → copy "token" into @token below
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "Admin@123" }

###
@token = paste-token-here

### Create employee (needs token)
POST {{api}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@demo.local",
  "phone": "+1-555-111-2222",
  "hireDate": "2025-01-15",
  "salary": 75000,
  "isActive": true,
  "employmentType": "FullTime",
  "departmentId": 1
}

### Validation error example (400)
POST {{api}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "", "email": "not-an-email", "departmentId": 0 }
